; The keyboard half of the motion pad, on the same reasoning as the tool belt's:
; the four buttons down the right-hand edge are the spec and are what ships,
; because the game is played in a browser on a phone — but nobody at a desk is
; going to reach for a button on screen to walk around a car.
;
; Both WASD and the arrow keys, two events on one action, because these are held
; rather than tapped: a hand that is already on the mouse wants the arrows and a
; hand that is not wants WASD, and an action is the right place for "either" to
; live. Physical keycodes again, so WASD stays a square block on a layout that
; prints different letters on those keys — which is the entire reason WASD is
; WASD.
;
; Up and down are the *eye's* height and not a look angle. There is deliberately
; no way to turn your head: see src/screens/play_screen.gd.

