[rendering]

; DECIDED (issue #13, when the web export landed): Forward+ on desktop,
; gl_compatibility on the web, and the engine — not this file — owns the split.
;
; The web half is not a preference. Godot 4.7.1 registers
; `rendering/renderer/rendering_method.web` itself, as a one-value enum whose
; only value is "gl_compatibility", with the source comment "This is a bit of a
; hack until we have WebGPU support" (main/main.cpp). Feature-tagged overrides
; beat the plain key, so a web build ignores the line below no matter what it
; says. Measured, not assumed: the exported bundle logs "OpenGL API OpenGL ES
; 3.0 (WebGL 2.0 ...) - Compatibility" in the browser console while this stays
; "forward_plus". There is no configuration to add and none to maintain.
;
; So we do run two renderers, and the cost is real: a Forward+-only feature
; (SDFGI, volumetric fog, SSIL/SSAO, the Vulkan-only bits of the sky and light
; pipeline) is simply absent from the build people click on. Nothing in the
; project uses one today — day 0 is a Label on a Control — which is why this is
; settled now rather than after visual work exists. The rule that comes with
; the decision, and the trigger to revisit it (drop desktop to gl_compatibility
; too), are in STANDARDS.md "Distribution".
;
; Redundant on purpose is what this line is NOT: it equals the engine default,
; and ProjectSettings::save_custom() skips any setting whose value matches its
; initial (`if (v->variant == v->initial) continue;`) — so the editor will drop
; it the first time anyone opens Project Settings, and dropping it changes
; nothing. Spelling out `renderer/rendering_method.web` here would be deleted
; the same way, which is why the decision is written down instead of typed out.
renderer/rendering_method="forward_plus"
